Example \(\PageIndex{3}\)

Solve: \(x^{2}+72=0\).

Solution:

            \(x^{2}+72=0\)	

            Isolate the quadratic term.	
            \(x^{2}=-72\)	

            Use the Square Root Property.	
            \(x=\pm \sqrt{-72}\)	

            Simplify using complex numbers.	
            \(x=\pm \sqrt{72} i\)	

            Simplify the radical.	
            \(x=\pm 6 \sqrt{2} i\)	

            Rewrite to show two solutions	
            \(x=6 \sqrt{2} i, x=-6 \sqrt{2} i\)	

Check the solutions:

\(\begin{array}{r}{x^{2}+72=0} 

            \\ {(\color{red}{6 \sqrt{2}i}\color{black}{)}^{2}+72 \stackrel{?}{=} 0} 

            \\ {\color{red}{(6)^2 \cdot (\sqrt{2})^2\cdot i^2}\color{black}+72 \stackrel{?}{=} 0} 

            \\ {36 \cdot 2\cdot(-1)+72 \stackrel{?}{=} 0} 

            \\ {0=0}\Large\color{\green}{\checkmark}\end{array}\)

\(\begin{array}{r}{x^{2}+72=0} 

            \\ {(\color{red}{-6 \sqrt{2}i}\color{black}{)}^{2}+72 \stackrel{?}{=} 0} 

            \\ {\color{red}{(-6)^2 \cdot (\sqrt{2})^2\cdot i^2}\color{black}+72 \stackrel{?}{=} 0} 

            \\ {36 \cdot 2\cdot(-1)+72 \stackrel{?}{=} 0} 

            \\ {0=0}\Large\color{\green}{\checkmark}\end{array}\)

    Table 9.1.3

